      "raw": "<p>When a hero becomes incapacitated, do all of their cards and all cards that were on them leave play?</p><p>Some specifics:&nbsp;</p><p>Chrono-Ranger&#39;s Bounties, AZ&#39;s Impale, or Vis&#39; Twist the Ether. This seems like an obvious discards according to the core rules. They may not be in front of that hero, but they are still one of their cards.</p><p>However, what about hero cards that are under other cards (e.g. La Capitan or Savage Mana)? Are those removed from play as well?</p><p>And here&#39;s the one that confused us today: if Isolated Hero was on the hero that becomes incapacitated, is it discarded? &nbsp;The general consensus in the forum seems to be that Isolated Hero can affect Incapcitated abilities, but as an incapactiated hero isn&#39;t a valid target anymore, would a villain card like that be discarded when the Hero character card flips?</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
