      "created_at": "2014-11-05T17:16:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>All of a hero's cards, regardless of where they are, leave play when the hero is incapped. Cards played on a hero only leave play if the card specifically says \"when the target leaves play, destroy this card.\"</p>\n<p>As an example, Infections do not have that phrase, therefore they are not destroyed when a hero is incapped.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's an interesting mechanic. I guess ultimately it wouldn't matter too much, since if it fails to infect a hero, you move on to what Rat's next card would be. So it's useless if there isn't an active hero to infect.</p>",
